{
  "info": {
    "name": "Sarfees — Group Trip (3 passengers, one driver)",
    "description": "Tests Stage-1 GROUPING: three separate passengers book the same corridor (Irbid → Amman) at the same departure time, the engine bundles them into ONE trip group, and one driver serves all of them in a single multi-stop trip.\n\n## How the timing works\n- Passenger A books a **scheduled** trip departing **now + 32 min** (a pre-request script computes this and shares it via `groupTravelDate`).\n- B and C book the same corridor/time within seconds — the group is still OPEN (freeze only happens at T-30), so they join A's group.\n- ~2 min later the sweeper freezes the group and cascades the offer to the top-ranked driver.\n\n## Why the pickup points are close together\nThe compatibility engine enforces a wait tolerance (default 12 min): adding a member is rejected if the extra pickup legs would delay an existing member past their tolerance (`wait_tolerance_exceeded`). The three pickups here are ~1 km apart so every insertion passes. Spread them across town and passenger C gets their own group instead — try it to see the rejection in the API logs.\n\n## ⚠️ If the driver's REAL mobile app is running\nThe driver app pings GPS every ~10 s, and every ping overwrites the matcher's location snapshot — it beats whatever `currentLocationLat/Lng` this collection sends in activate. The cascade hard-filters drivers to the ORIGIN city, so **the trip's departure city must be the city where the driver's phone physically is**, or the driver is silently excluded and the offer goes to other drivers (then escalates). This collection books **Irbid → Amman** with pickups in north Irbid; if you're testing from Amman (or with no real app open), flip `departureCityId`/`arrivalCityId` and swap the departure/arrival coordinates.\n\n## Run order\n1. **Auth** — OTP logins for passengers A/B/C and the driver (mock OTP `1234`).\n2. **Driver online** — activate with GPS in the pickup area.\n3. **Passengers book** — A creates the group, B and C join it. Run 3.1 → 3.2 → 3.3 back-to-back (within the ~2 min OPEN window).\n4. **Matching** — re-run 4.1 every ~30 s until `pendingOffer` appears (expect ~2-3 min because of the T-30 freeze). Offer has a 30 s countdown — accept promptly.\n5. **Assign** — accept returns the manifest. Test asserts `summary.passengerCount === 3` (grouping proof) and saves the ordered stop list.\n6. **Execute** — generic loop: `6.2 Arrive at CURRENT stop` then `6.3a/6.3b Confirm` (pickup or dropoff — console tells you which). Repeat 6.2 → confirm for every stop, then complete.\n\n## Prereqs\n- Seeded passengers `790000001/2/3` + driver `770000001` (Contabo test data).\n- Driver has no leftover active trip.\n- Responses are wrapped `{ code, message, data }`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://169.58.67.105" },
    { "key": "countryCode", "value": "+962" },
    { "key": "otp", "value": "1234" },
    { "key": "passengerAPhone", "value": "790000001" },
    { "key": "passengerBPhone", "value": "790000002" },
    { "key": "passengerCPhone", "value": "790000003" },
    { "key": "driverPhone", "value": "770000001" },
    { "key": "passengerAToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "passengerBToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "passengerCToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "driverToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "groupTravelDate", "value": "" },
    { "key": "requestAId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "requestBId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "requestCId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "driverTripId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "stopsJson", "value": "[]" },
    { "key": "currentStopIndex", "value": "0" },
    { "key": "currentStopId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "currentPickupIds", "value": "[]" },
    { "key": "currentDropoffEntries", "value": "[]" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Auth — 3 passengers + driver",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1.1 Passenger A — request OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{passengerAPhone}}\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"{{countryCode}}\"\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('OTP requested', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.2 Passenger A — verify OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{passengerAPhone}}\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"{{countryCode}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.collectionVariables.set('passengerAToken', d.accessToken);",
            "pm.test('A token saved', () => pm.expect(d.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.3 Passenger B — request OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{passengerBPhone}}\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"{{countryCode}}\"\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('OTP requested', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.4 Passenger B — verify OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{passengerBPhone}}\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"{{countryCode}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.collectionVariables.set('passengerBToken', d.accessToken);",
            "pm.test('B token saved', () => pm.expect(d.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.5 Passenger C — request OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{passengerCPhone}}\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"{{countryCode}}\"\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('OTP requested', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.6 Passenger C — verify OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{passengerCPhone}}\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"{{countryCode}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.collectionVariables.set('passengerCToken', d.accessToken);",
            "pm.test('C token saved', () => pm.expect(d.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.7 Driver — request OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/driver/request-otp",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{driverPhone}}\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"{{countryCode}}\"\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('OTP requested', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "1.8 Driver — verify OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/driver/verify-otp",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"{{driverPhone}}\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"{{countryCode}}\",\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.collectionVariables.set('driverToken', d.accessToken);",
            "pm.test('driver token saved', () => pm.expect(d.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));"
          ] } }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Driver goes online",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "2.1 Activate (GPS at pickup area, dest Irbid)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{driverToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/drivers/activate",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"tripTypes\": [\"mixed\"],\n  \"goingHome\": false,\n  \"destinationCity\": \"Amman\",\n  \"minPassengers\": 1,\n  \"currentLocationLat\": 32.5808,\n  \"currentLocationLng\": 35.8661\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.test('driver is active', () => pm.expect(d.status).to.eql('active'));"
          ] } }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Passengers book — same corridor, same departure",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "3.1 Passenger A books (creates the group, T+32 min)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{passengerAToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/trips/request",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"departureCityId\": 2,\n  \"arrivalCityId\": 1,\n  \"departureLocation\": { \"lat\": 32.5810, \"lng\": 35.8660 },\n  \"arrivalLocation\": { \"lat\": 31.9612, \"lng\": 35.8776 },\n  \"travelDate\": \"{{groupTravelDate}}\",\n  \"seatsCount\": 1\n}" },
            "description": "Scheduled 32 min out: the group is born OPEN and stays joinable until T-30 (~2 min). Run 3.2 and 3.3 immediately after. Pickups are in north Irbid, right where the demo driver's phone is."
          },
          "event": [
            { "listen": "prerequest", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "const dep = new Date(Date.now() + 32 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('groupTravelDate', dep);",
              "console.log('Group departure set to', dep, '— B and C reuse it. Freeze fires at T-30 (~2 min from now).');"
            ] } },
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('requestAId', d.id);",
              "pm.test('A request created', () => pm.expect(d.id).to.exist);",
              "console.log('Request A =', d.id, '— now run 3.2 and 3.3 quickly.');"
            ] } }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3.2 Passenger B joins (nearby pickup, same time)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{passengerBToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/trips/request",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"departureCityId\": 2,\n  \"arrivalCityId\": 1,\n  \"departureLocation\": { \"lat\": 32.5790, \"lng\": 35.8680 },\n  \"arrivalLocation\": { \"lat\": 31.9560, \"lng\": 35.8850 },\n  \"travelDate\": \"{{groupTravelDate}}\",\n  \"seatsCount\": 1\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.collectionVariables.set('requestBId', d.id);",
            "pm.test('B request created', () => pm.expect(d.id).to.exist);"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "3.3 Passenger C joins (nearby pickup, same time)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{passengerCToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/trips/request",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"departureCityId\": 2,\n  \"arrivalCityId\": 1,\n  \"departureLocation\": { \"lat\": 32.5820, \"lng\": 35.8640 },\n  \"arrivalLocation\": { \"lat\": 31.9530, \"lng\": 35.8900 },\n  \"travelDate\": \"{{groupTravelDate}}\",\n  \"seatsCount\": 1\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.collectionVariables.set('requestCId', d.id);",
            "pm.test('C request created', () => pm.expect(d.id).to.exist);",
            "console.log('All three requests in. Freeze + driver search fires when departure crosses T-30 (~2 min). Then poll 4.1.');"
          ] } }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Matching — wait for the group offer",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "4.1 Poll driver home-summary → pendingOffer (re-run until pass)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{driverToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/drivers/home-summary",
            "description": "Freeze happens when the shared departure crosses T-30 (~2 min after booking), then the cascade offers the trip. RE-RUN every ~30 s until the test passes. The offer has a 30 s countdown — accept promptly once it appears."
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "const offer = d.pendingOffer;",
            "if (offer) {",
            "  pm.collectionVariables.set('driverTripId', offer.tripId ?? offer.id);",
            "  console.log('Offer! DriverTrip', offer.tripId, '—', offer.secondsRemaining, 's left. Run 4.2 then 5.1 NOW.');",
            "} else {",
            "  console.log('No offer yet — group freezes at T-30, sweeper ticks every 30 s. Re-run.');",
            "}",
            "pm.test('pendingOffer present (re-run until it passes)', () => pm.expect(offer, 'pendingOffer').to.exist);"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "4.2 Offer details — passenger count shows the bundle",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{driverToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/drivers/trips/{{driverTripId}}/offer"
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "console.log('Offer summary:', JSON.stringify(d).slice(0, 400));",
            "pm.test('offer returned', () => pm.response.to.be.success);"
          ] } }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Assign — accept, PROOF of grouping",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "5.1 Accept → manifest must contain all 3 passengers",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{driverToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/drivers/trips/{{driverTripId}}/accept"
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "const stops = (d.stops || []).sort((a, b) => a.order - b.order);",
            "pm.collectionVariables.set('stopsJson', JSON.stringify(stops));",
            "pm.collectionVariables.set('currentStopIndex', '0');",
            "pm.test('GROUPING PROOF: 3 passengers on one trip', () =>",
            "  pm.expect(d.summary.passengerCount, 'summary.passengerCount').to.eql(3));",
            "pm.test('multi-stop itinerary (>= 2 pickups + dropoffs)', () =>",
            "  pm.expect(stops.length, 'stop count').to.be.at.least(2));",
            "console.log('Itinerary (' + stops.length + ' stops):');",
            "stops.forEach((s, i) => console.log('  ' + i + '. #' + s.id + ' ' + s.type + ' @ ' + s.lat + ',' + s.lng + ' — passengers: ' + s.passengers.map(p => p.name).join(', ')));",
            "console.log('Now run 6.1 start, then loop 6.2 arrive → 6.3a/6.3b confirm per stop.');"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "5.2 Passenger A sees the assigned driver",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{passengerAToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/trips/{{requestAId}}/status"
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.test('A has a driver', () => pm.expect(d.driver, 'driver').to.exist);",
            "console.log('A driver:', d.driver && d.driver.name);"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "5.3 Passenger B sees the SAME driver",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{passengerBToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/trips/{{requestBId}}/status"
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.test('B has a driver', () => pm.expect(d.driver, 'driver').to.exist);",
            "console.log('B driver:', d.driver && d.driver.name);"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "5.4 Passenger C sees the SAME driver",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{passengerCToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/trips/{{requestCId}}/status"
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.test('C has a driver', () => pm.expect(d.driver, 'driver').to.exist);",
            "console.log('C driver:', d.driver && d.driver.name);"
          ] } }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Execute — multi-stop loop, start to finish",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "6.1 Start trip",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{driverToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/drivers/trips/{{driverTripId}}/start"
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "pm.test('trip started', () => pm.response.to.be.success);",
            "const stops = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('stopsJson'));",
            "console.log('First stop is #' + stops[0].id + ' (' + stops[0].type + '). Run 6.2.');"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.2 Arrive at CURRENT stop (repeat per stop)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{driverToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/drivers/trips/{{driverTripId}}/stops/{{currentStopId}}/arrive",
            "description": "Pre-request script resolves the current stop from the saved itinerary. After it succeeds, run 6.3a (pickup stop) or 6.3b (dropoff stop) — the console tells you which."
          },
          "event": [
            { "listen": "prerequest", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "const stops = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('stopsJson'));",
              "const i = parseInt(pm.collectionVariables.get('currentStopIndex'), 10);",
              "const stop = stops[i];",
              "if (!stop) throw new Error('No stop at index ' + i + ' — all stops done? Run 6.4 complete.');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('currentStopId', stop.id);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('currentPickupIds', JSON.stringify(stop.passengers.map(p => p.id)));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('currentDropoffEntries', JSON.stringify(stop.passengers.map(p => ({ id: p.id, cashCollected: true }))));",
              "console.log('Arriving at stop ' + i + ' (#' + stop.id + ', ' + stop.type + ') — next run 6.3' + (stop.type === 'pickup' ? 'a (confirm pickup)' : 'b (confirm dropoff)'));"
            ] } },
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('arrived', () => pm.response.to.be.success);"] } }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.3a Confirm PICKUP at current stop",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{driverToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/drivers/trips/{{driverTripId}}/stops/{{currentStopId}}/confirm-pickup",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"passengersPickedUp\": {{currentPickupIds}},\n  \"noShows\": []\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "pm.test('pickup confirmed', () => pm.response.to.be.success);",
            "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
            "  const stops = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('stopsJson'));",
            "  const next = parseInt(pm.collectionVariables.get('currentStopIndex'), 10) + 1;",
            "  pm.collectionVariables.set('currentStopIndex', String(next));",
            "  if (stops[next]) console.log('Next: stop ' + next + ' (#' + stops[next].id + ', ' + stops[next].type + ') — run 6.2 again.');",
            "  else console.log('All stops handled — run 6.4 complete.');",
            "}"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.3b Confirm DROPOFF at current stop (cash)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{driverToken}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/drivers/trips/{{driverTripId}}/stops/{{currentStopId}}/confirm-dropoff",
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"passengersDroppedOff\": {{currentDropoffEntries}},\n  \"packagesDelivered\": []\n}" }
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "pm.test('dropoff confirmed', () => pm.response.to.be.success);",
            "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
            "  const stops = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('stopsJson'));",
            "  const next = parseInt(pm.collectionVariables.get('currentStopIndex'), 10) + 1;",
            "  pm.collectionVariables.set('currentStopIndex', String(next));",
            "  if (stops[next]) console.log('Next: stop ' + next + ' (#' + stops[next].id + ', ' + stops[next].type + ') — run 6.2 again.');",
            "  else console.log('All stops handled — run 6.4 complete.');",
            "}"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.4 Complete trip → earnings for the whole group",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{driverToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/drivers/trips/{{driverTripId}}/complete"
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "pm.test('trip completed', () => pm.response.to.be.success);",
            "pm.test('served all 3 passengers', () => pm.expect(d.passengersServed).to.eql(3));",
            "console.log('Earnings:', JSON.stringify(d, null, 2));"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.5 Passenger A history — COMPLETED",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{passengerAToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/trips/my-trips"
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "const rows = d.data ?? d;",
            "const mine = rows.find(t => t.id === parseInt(pm.collectionVariables.get('requestAId'), 10));",
            "pm.test('A request COMPLETED', () => pm.expect(mine && mine.status).to.eql('COMPLETED'));"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.6 Passenger B history — COMPLETED",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{passengerBToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/trips/my-trips"
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "const rows = d.data ?? d;",
            "const mine = rows.find(t => t.id === parseInt(pm.collectionVariables.get('requestBId'), 10));",
            "pm.test('B request COMPLETED', () => pm.expect(mine && mine.status).to.eql('COMPLETED'));"
          ] } }]
        },
        {
          "name": "6.7 Passenger C history — COMPLETED",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{passengerCToken}}" }],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/trips/my-trips"
          },
          "event": [{ "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
            "const d = pm.response.json().data ?? pm.response.json();",
            "const rows = d.data ?? d;",
            "const mine = rows.find(t => t.id === parseInt(pm.collectionVariables.get('requestCId'), 10));",
            "pm.test('C request COMPLETED', () => pm.expect(mine && mine.status).to.eql('COMPLETED'));"
          ] } }]
        }
      ]
    }
